{
  "title": "Fifteenth Night of Shaban",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "This night is extraordinarily honorable. Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a) narrates that when Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a) was asked about the merits of the fifteenth night of Shaban, he said: \"It is the most favorable night after the Night of Decree. On it, Almighty Allah bestows His favors upon His servants and grants pardon out of His own bounty; so exert every effort to seek nearness to Him this night, for He — Majestic and Honorable — has decided not to turn away any asker so long as he does not ask for an act of disobedience. Allah has chosen this night for us, the Ahl al-Bayt, just as He chose the Night of Decree for our Prophet — peace be upon him and his Household. So pray and give thanks diligently.\"\nOne of the marvelous blessings of this night is that it is the birth night of the Patron of the Age, Imam al-Mahdi (a) — may Allah accept our souls as ransom for him. He was born in Surra-man-ra'a (Samarra) just before daybreak in 255 AH, which only increases the merit of this honorable night. Narrations record many recommended rites for this night:\nFirst: it is highly recommended to bathe, for this act lessens the punishment for one's sins.\nSecond: it is highly recommended to imitate Imam Ali ibn al-Husayn, Zayn al-Abidin (a), who used to spend this whole night in worship, prayer, supplication, and seeking forgiveness. A tradition confirms that whoever spends this whole night in worship, his heart will not die when other hearts die.\nThird: it is highly recommended to visit the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a) — the most favorable act of this night, bringing forgiveness of one's sins; whoever desires that 124,000 Prophets shake his hand may visit the holy tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a) this night. The least form of this Ziyarah is to stand on elevated ground, look right and left, raise the head to the sky, and say:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَبَا عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَ رَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَ بَرَكَاتُهُ\nASSALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ABAA A'BDIL LAAH ASSALAAMU A'LAYKA WA RAHMATUL LAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, O Abu Abdillah; peace be upon you, and Allah's mercy and blessings.\nWhoever performs even this form of Ziyarah is expected to win the reward of a Hajj and an Umrah.\nFourth: it is recommended to say the following, which stands as a form of Ziyarah for Imam al-Mahdi (a), mentioned by both Sayyid Ibn Tawus and Shaykh al-Tusi:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ بِحَقِّ لَيْلَتِنَا هٰذِهِ وَ مَوْلُوْدِهَا وَ حُجَّتِكَ وَ مَوْعُوْدِهَا الَّتِيْ قَرَنْتَ اِلٰى فَضْلِهَا فَضْلًا فَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَتُكَ صِدْقًا وَ عَدْلًا لَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمَاتِكَ وَ لَا مُعَقِّبَ لِاٰيَاتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA BI-HAQQI LAYLATINAA HAAZIHI WA MAWLOODIHAA WA HUJJATIKA WA MAW-U'WDIHAA-LLATEE QARANTA ILAA FADLIHAA FADLAA, FATAMMAT KALIMATUKA SIDQAW WA A'DLAA, LAA MUBADDILA LI-KALIMAATIK WA LAA MU-A'QQIBA LI-AAYAATIK\nO Allah, by the right of this night of ours, and its Newborn, and Your Proof and its Promised One — the night to whose merit You have joined further merit, so Your Word was fulfilled in truth and justice; none can alter Your words, and none can pursue Your signs;\nنُوْرُكَ الْمُتَاَلِّقُ وَ ضِيَاۤؤُكَ الْمُشْرِقُ وَ الْعَلَمُ النُّوْرُ فِيْ طَخْيَاۤءِ الدَّيْجُوْرِ الْغَاۤئِبُ الْمَسْتُوْرُ\nNOORUKAL MUTA-ALLIQ WA DIYAAA-UKAL MUSHRIQ WAL A'LAMUN NOORU FEE TAKHYAAA-ID DAYJOOR AL-GHAAA-IBUL MASTOOR\nhe is Your radiant light, Your shining brightness, the luminous banner amid the pitch darkness — the hidden, the veiled one,\nجَلَّ مَوْلِدُهُ وَ كَرُمَ مَحْتِدُهُ وَ الْمَلَاۤئِكَةُ شُهَّدُهُ وَ اللّٰهُ نَاصِرُهُ وَ مُؤَيِّدُهُ اِذَا اٰنَ مِيْعَادُهُ وَ الْمَلَاۤئِكَةُ اَمْدَادُهُ\nJALLA MAWLIDUHU WA KARUMA MAHTIDUH, WAL MALAAA-IKATU SHUHHADUH, WALLAAHO NAASIRUHU WA MU-AYYIDUH, IZAA AANA MEE-A'ADUHU WAL MALAAA-IKATU AMDAADUH\nlofty is his birth and noble his lineage, the angels are his witnesses, and Allah is his helper and supporter; when his appointed time arrives, the angels shall be his reinforcements,\nسَيْفُ اللّٰهِ الَّذِيْ لَا يَنْبُوْ وَ نُوْرُهُ الَّذِيْ لَا يَخْبُوْ وَ ذُوْ الْحِلْمِ الَّذِيْ لَا يَصْبُوْ\nSAYFUL LAAHIL LAZEE LAA YANBOO WA NOORUHUL LAZEE LAA YAKHBOO WA ZUL HILMIL LAZEE LAA YASBOO\nhe is the sword of Allah that never fails, His light that never dims, and the possessor of forbearance who never inclines to folly,\nمَدَارُ الدَّهْرِ وَ نَوَامِيْسُ الْعَصْرِ وَ وُلَاةُ الْاَمْرِ وَ الْمُنَزَّلُ عَلَيْهِمْ مَا يَتَنَزَّلُ فِيْ لَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ\nMADAARUD DAHRI WA NAWAAMEESUL A'SRI WA WULAATUL AMRI WAL MUNAZZALU A'LAYHIM MAA YATANAZZALU FEE LAYLATIL QADR\nthe pivot of time, the laws of the age, the holders of authority, upon whom descends what is sent down on the Night of Decree,\nوَ اَصْحَابُ الْحَشْرِ وَ النَّشْرِ تَرَاجِمَةُ وَحْيِهِ وَ وُلَاةُ اَمْرِهِ وَ نَهْيِهِ\nWA ASHAABUL HASHRI WAN NASHRI TARAAJIMATU WAHYIH WA WULAATU AMRIHI WA NAHYIH\nand the masters of the Gathering and the Resurrection, the interpreters of His revelation and the executors of His command and His prohibition.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَصَلِّ عَلٰى خَاتِمِهِمْ وَ قَاۤئِمِهِمُ الْمَسْتُوْرِ عَنْ عَوَالِمِهِمْ\nALLAAHUMMA FASALLI A'LAA KHAATIMIHIM WA QAAA-IMIHIMUL MASTOORI A'N A'WAALIMIHIM\nO Allah, so bless their seal and their Riser, hidden from their worlds,\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ اَدْرِكْ بِنَاۤ اَيَّامَهُ وَ ظُهُوْرَهُ وَ قِيَامَهُ وَ اجْعَلْنَا مِنْ اَنْصَارِهِ وَ اقْرِنْ ثَارَنَا بِثَارِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA WA ADRIK BINAAA AYYAAMAHU WA ZUHOORAHU WA QIYAAMAH, WAJ-A'LNAA MIN ANSAARIH, WAQRIN THAARANAA BI-THAARIH\nO Allah, let us reach his days, his manifestation, and his rising; make us among his supporters; join our claim for retribution with his,\nوَ اكْتُبْنَا فِيْۤ اَعْوَانِهِ وَ خُلَصَاۤئِهِ وَ اَحْيِنَا فِيْ دَوْلَتِهِ نَاعِمِيْنَ وَ بِصُحْبَتِهِ غَانِمِيْنَ وَ بِحَقِّهِ قَاۤئِمِيْنَ وَ مِنَ السُّوْۤءِ سَالِمِيْنَ\nWAKTUBNAA FEE A'WAANIHI WA KHULASAAA-IH, WA AHYINAA FEE DAWLATIHI NAA-I'MEEN, WA BI-SUHBATIHI GHAANIMEEN, WA BI-HAQQIHI QAAA-IMEEN, WA MINAS SOOO-I SAALIMEEN\nand record us among his helpers and his intimates; let us live in his rule in bliss, gaining through his company, upholding his right, and safe from all harm — O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nوَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ وَ صَلَوَاتُهُ عَلٰى سَيِّدِنَا مُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ وَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ وَ عَلٰى اَهْلِ بَيْتِهِ الصَّادِقِيْنَ وَ عِتْرَتِهِ النَّاطِقِيْنَ وَ الْعَنْ جَمِيْعَ الظَّالِمِيْنَ وَ احْكُمْ بَيْنَنَا وَ بَيْنَهُمْ يَاۤ اَحْكَمَ الْحَاكِمِيْنَ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN, WA SALAWAATUHU A'LAA SAYYIDINAA MUHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA WAL MURSALEEN, WA A'LAA AHLI BAYTIHIS SAADIQEEN WA I'TRATIHIN NAATIQEEN, WAL A'N JAMEE-A'Z ZAALIMEEN, WAHKUM BAYNANAA WA BAYNAHUM YAA AHKAMAL HAAKIMEEN\nAnd praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, and His blessings upon our master Muhammad, the seal of the Prophets and Messengers, and upon his truthful Household and his eloquent progeny; and curse all wrongdoers, and judge between us and them, O Most Just of judges.\nFifth: Shaykh Isma'il ibn Fadl al-Hashimi reports that Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a) instructed him to say this on the fifteenth night of Shaban:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّوْمُ الْعَلِيُّ الْعَظِيْمُ الْخَالِقُ الرَّازِقُ الْمُحْيِيْ الْمُمِيْتُ الْبَدِيْۤءُ الْبَدِيْعُ\nALLAAHUMMA ANTAL HAYYUL QAYYOOM, AL-A'LIYYUL A'ZEEM, AL-KHAALIQUR RAAZIQ, AL-MUHYIL MUMEET, AL-BADEE-O'L BADEE'\nO Allah, You are the Ever-living, the Self-subsisting, the Most High, the All-magnificent, the Creator, the Sustainer, the Giver of life, the Bringer of death, the Beginner, the Innovator;\nلَكَ الْجَلَالُ وَ لَكَ الْفَضْلُ وَ لَكَ الْحَمْدُ وَ لَكَ الْمَنُّ وَ لَكَ الْجُوْدُ وَ لَكَ الْكَرَمُ وَ لَكَ الْاَمْرُ وَ لَكَ الْمَجْدُ وَ لَكَ الشُّكْرُ وَحْدَكَ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَكَ\nLAKAL JALAAL, WA LAKAL FADL, WA LAKAL HAMD, WA LAKAL MANN, WA LAKAL JOOD, WA LAKAL KARAM, WA LAKAL AMR, WA LAKAL MAJD, WA LAKASH SHUKR, WAHDAKA LAA SHAREEKA LAK\nYours is the majesty, Yours the bounty, Yours the praise, Yours the favor, Yours the generosity, Yours the nobility, Yours the command, Yours the glory, and Yours the thanks, alone, with no partner unto You;\nيَا وَاحِدُ يَا اَحَدُ يَا صَمَدُ يَا مَنْ لَمْ يَلِدْ وَ لَمْ يُوْلَدْ وَ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُ كُفُوًا اَحَدٌ\nYAA WAAHIDO YAA AHADO YAA SAMADO YAA MAL LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD WA LAM YAKUL LAHU KUFUWAN AHAD\nO One, O Only, O Self-sufficient, O He Who has not begotten and was not begotten, and there is none comparable to Him.\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اغْفِرْ لِيْ وَ ارْحَمْنِيْ وَ اكْفِنِيْ مَاۤ اَهَمَّنِيْ وَ اقْضِ دَيْنِيْ وَ وَسِّعْ عَلَيَّ فِيْ رِزْقِيْ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIW WA AALI MUHAMMAD, WAGH FIR LEE WARHAMNEE WAKFINEE MAAA AHAMMANEE, WAQDI DAYNEE, WA WASSI' A'LAYYA FEE RIZQEE\nBless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, forgive me, have mercy on me, spare me what worries me, settle my debt, and expand my sustenance for me,\nفَاِنَّكَ فِيْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ كُلَّ اَمْرٍ حَكِيْمٍ تَفْرُقُ وَ مَنْ تَشَاۤءُ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ تَرْزُقُ فَارْزُقْنِيْ وَ اَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرَّازِقِيْنَ\nFA-INNAKA FEE HAAZIHIL LAYLATI KULLA AMRIN HAKEEMIN TAFRUQ, WA MAN TASHAAA-O MIN KHALQIKA TARZUQ, FARZUQNEE WA ANTA KHAYRUR RAAZIQEEN\nfor on this night You distinguish every wise matter, and You provide for whomever You will among Your creatures; so provide for me, for You are the Best of providers.\nفَاِنَّكَ قُلْتَ وَ اَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْقَاۤئِلِيْنَ وَالنَّاطِقِيْنَ وَ اسْئَلُوْا اللّٰهَ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ فَمِنْ فَضْلِكَ اَسْاَلُ\nFA-INNAKA QULTA WA ANTA KHAYRUL QAAA-ILEENA WAN NAATIQEEN, WAS-ALUL LAAHA MIN FADLIH, FAMIN FADLIKA AS-AL\nFor You have said — and You are the Best of speakers — \"Ask Allah of His bounty\"; so of Your bounty I ask,\nوَ اِيَّاكَ قَصَدْتُ وَ ابْنَ نَبِيِّكَ اعْتَمَدْتُ وَ لَكَ رَجَوْتُ فَارْحَمْنِيْ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nWA IYYAAKA QASADT, WABNA NABIYYIKA A'TAMADT, WA LAKA RAJAWT, FARHAMNEE YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nand toward You I have directed myself, and upon the son of Your Prophet I have relied, and in You I have hoped; so have mercy on me, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nSixth: it is recommended to say this, which the Holy Prophet (s) used to say on this night — one of the perfect, comprehensive prayers said at all times, per the book Awali al-La'ali:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اقْسِمْ لَنَا مِنْ خَشْيَتِكَ مَا يَحُوْلُ بَيْنَنَا وَ بَيْنَ مَعْصِيَتِكَ وَ مِنْ طَاعَتِكَ مَا تُبَلِّغُنَا بِهِ رِضْوَانَكَ وَ مِنَ الْيَقِيْنِ مَا يَهُوْنُ عَلَيْنَا بِهِ مُصِيْبَاتُ الدُّنْيَا\nALLAAHUMMAQ SIM LANAA MIN KHASHYATIKA MAA YAHOOLU BAYNANAA WA BAYNA MA'SIYATIK, WA MIN TAA-A'TIKA MAA TUBALLIGHUNAA BIHI RIDWAANAK, WA MINAL YAQEENI MAA YAHOONU A'LAYNAA BIHI MUSEEBAATUD DUNYAA\nO Allah, apportion for us of Your fear that which comes between us and disobedience to You, and of Your obedience that which brings us to Your good pleasure, and of certainty that which makes the calamities of this world light upon us,\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَمْتِعْنَا بِاَسْمَاعِنَا وَ اَبْصَارِنَا وَ قُوَّتِنَا مَاۤ اَحْيَيْتَنَا وَ اجْعَلْهُ الْوَارِثَ مِنَّا\nALLAAHUMMA AMTI-A'NAA BI-ASMAA-A'NAA WA ABSAARINAA WA QUWWATINAA MAA AHYAYTANAA, WAJ-A'LHUL WAARISA MINNAA\nO Allah, let us enjoy our hearing, our sight, and our strength for as long as You keep us alive, and make them what outlasts us,\nوَ اجْعَلْ ثَارَنَا عَلٰى مَنْ ظَلَمَنَا وَ انْصُرْنَا عَلٰى مَنْ عَادَانَا وَ لَا تَجْعَلْ مُصِيْبَتَنَا فِيْ دِيْنِنَا\nWAJ-A'L THAARANAA A'LAA MAN ZALAMANAA, WANSURNAA A'LAA MAN A'ADAANAA, WA LAA TAJ-A'L MUSEEBATANAA FEE DEENINAA\ngrant us retribution against whoever wrongs us, give us victory over whoever is hostile to us, and do not let our affliction be in our religion,\nوَ لَا تَجْعَلِ الدُّنْيَا اَكْبَرَ هَمِّنَا وَ لَا مَبْلَغَ عِلْمِنَا وَ لَا تُسَلِّطْ عَلَيْنَا مَنْ لَا يَرْحَمُنَا بِرَحْمَتِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nWA LAA TAJ-A'LID DUNYAA AKBARA HAMMINAA WA LAA MABLAGHA I'LMINAA, WA LAA TUSALLIT A'LAYNAA MAL LAA YARHAMUNAA, BI-RAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nand do not make the world our greatest concern nor the sum of our knowledge, and do not let anyone rule over us who has no mercy on us — by Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nSeventh: it is recommended to say the prayers dedicated to midday, mentioned earlier in this book, which begin \"O Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, the tree of Prophethood and the place of the Message...\" (the source record available here ends at this opening line).\nEighth: it is recommended to say the famous [Dua Kumayl](E31), which narrations especially recommend for this night.\nNinth: it is recommended to repeat the following litany a hundred times, so that past disobedience is forgiven and worldly and religious needs are granted:\nسُبْحَانَ اللهِ وَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَ اللهُ اَكْبَرُ وَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHI WAL HAMDU LILLAAHI WALLAAHO AKBAR WA LAA ILAAHA ILLAL LAAH\nGlory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, Allah is the Greatest, and there is no god but Allah.\nTenth: Shaykh al-Tusi, in Misbah al-Mutahajjid, narrates that Abu-Yahya asked Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a) about the best supplication for this night. The Imam instructed him: after the obligatory Isha prayer, offer a two-unit prayer — in the first unit [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) and [Surah al-Kafirun](A113), in the second Surah al-Faatehah and [Surah al-Ikhlas](A116). On finishing, repeat \"SubhanAllah\" thirty-three times, \"Alhamdulillah\" thirty-three times, and \"Allahu Akbar\" thirty-four times, then say:\nيَا مَنْ اِلَيْهِ مَلْجَاُ الْعِبَادِ فِي الْمُهِمَّاتِ وَ اِلَيْهِ يَفْزَعُ الْخَلْقُ فِي الْمُلِمَّاتِ\nYAA MAN ILAYHI MALJA-UL I'BAADI FIL MUHIMMAAT, WA ILAYHI YAFZA-U'L KHALQU FIL MULIMMAAT\nO He to Whom servants turn for refuge in urgent matters, and to Whom creation flees in calamities,\nيَا عَالِمَ الْجَهْرِ وَ الْخَفِيَّاتِ يَا مَنْ لَا تَخْفٰى عَلَيْهِ خَوَاطِرُ الْاَوْهَامِ وَ تَصَرُّفُ الْخَطَرَاتِ\nYAA A'ALIMAL JAHRI WAL KHAFIYYAAT, YAA MAL LAA TAKHFAA A'LAYHI KHAWAATIRUL AWHAAMI WA TASARRUFUL KHATARAAT\nO Knower of the open and the hidden, O He from Whom the passing thoughts of illusion and the shifting of ideas are not concealed,\nيَا رَبَّ الْخَلَاۤئِقِ وَ الْبَرِيَّاتِ يَا مَنْ بِيَدِهِ مَلَكُوْتُ الْاَرَضِيْنَ وَ السَّمَاوَاتِ\nYAA RABBAL KHALAAA-IQI WAL BARIYYAAT, YAA MAM BI-YADIHI MALAKOOTUL ARADEENA WAS SAMAAWAAT\nO Lord of all creatures and beings, O He in Whose hand is the dominion of the earths and the heavens,\nاَنْتَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ اَمُتُّ اِلَيْكَ بِلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ فَيَا لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ\nANTAL LAAHO LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT, AMUTTU ILAYKA BI-LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT, FA-YAA LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nYou are Allah, there is no god but You; I connect myself to You by \"there is no god but You\"; so O He besides Whom there is no god,\nاجْعَلْنِيْ فِيْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ مِمَّنْ نَظَرْتَ اِلَيْهِ فَرَحِمْتَهُ وَ سَمِعْتَ دُعَاۤءَهُ فَاَجَبْتَهُ وَ عَلِمْتَ اسْتِقَالَتَهُ فَاَقَلْتَهُ وَ تَجَاوَزْتَ عَنْ سَالِفِ خَطِيْۤئَتِهِ وَ عَظِيْمِ جَرِيْرَتِهِ\nIJ-A'LNEE FEE HAAZIHIL LAYLATI MIMMAN NAZARTA ILAYHI FARAHIMTAH, WA SAMI'TA DU-A'AA-AHU FA-AJABTAH, WA A'LIMTAS TIQAALATAHU FA-AQALTAH, WA TAJAAWAZTA A'N SAALIFI KHATEE-ATIHI WA A'ZEEMI JAREERATIH\nmake me, this night, among those upon whom You have looked with mercy, whose supplication You have heard and answered, whose plea for release You have known and granted, and whose past sins and grave offenses You have overlooked.\nفَقَدِ اسْتَجَرْتُ بِكَ مِنْ ذُنُوْبِيْ وَ لَجَأْتُ اِلَيْكَ فِيْ سَتْرِ عُيُوْبِيْ\nFAQADIS TAJARTU BIKA MIN ZUNOOBEE WA LAJA-TU ILAYKA FEE SATRI U'YOOBEE\nI have indeed taken refuge in You from my sins, and have taken shelter in You for the covering of my faults.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَجُدْ عَلَيَّ بِكَرَمِكَ وَ فَضْلِكَ وَ احْطُطْ خَطَايَايَ بِحِلْمِكَ وَ عَفْوِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA FAJUD A'LAYYA BI-KARAMIKA WA FADLIK, WAHTUT KHATAAYAAYA BI-HILMIKA WA A'FWIK\nO Allah, be generous to me with Your nobility and bounty, and remove my sins by Your forbearance and pardon,\nوَ تَغَمَّدْنِيْ فِيْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ بِسَابِغِ كَرَامَتِكَ وَ اجْعَلْنِيْ فِيْهَا مِنْ اَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اجْتَبَيْتَهُمْ لِطَاعَتِكَ وَ اخْتَرْتَهُمْ لِعِبَادَتِكَ وَ جَعَلْتَهُمْ خَالِصَتَكَ وَ صَفْوَتَكَ\nWA TAGHAMMADNEE FEE HAAZIHIL LAYLATI BI-SAABIGHI KARAAMATIK, WAJ-A'LNEE FEEHAA MIN AWLIYAAA-IKAL LAZEENAJ TABAYTAHUM LI-TAA-A'TIK, WAKH TARTAHUM LI-I'BAADATIK, WA JA-A'LTAHUM KHAALISATAKA WA SAFWATAK\nand envelop me this night with Your abundant honor, and make me, in it, among Your friends whom You have selected for Your obedience, chosen for Your worship, and made Your own elite and pure ones.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ سَعَدَ جَدُّهُ وَ تَوَفَّرَ مِنَ الْخَيْرَاتِ حَظُّهُ وَ اجْعَلْنِيْ مِمَّنْ سَلِمَ فَنَعِمَ وَ فَازَ فَغَنِمَ\nALLAAHUMMAJ-A'LNEE MIMMAN SA-I'DA JADDUH, WA TAWAFFARA MINAL KHAYRAATI HAZZUH, WAJ-A'LNEE MIMMAN SALIMA FANA-I'MA WA FAAZA FAGHANIM\nO Allah, make me among those whose fortune is blessed, whose share of good is abundant, and make me among those who are spared and so are blessed, who succeed and so gain,\nوَ اكْفِنِيْ شَرَّ مَاۤ اَسْلَفْتُ وَ اعْصِمْنِيْ مِنَ الْاِزْدِيَادِ فِيْ مَعْصِيَتِكَ وَ حَبِّبْ اِلَيَّ طَاعَتَكَ وَ مَا يُقَرِّبُنِيْ مِنْكَ وَ يُزْلِفُنِيْ عِنْدَكَ\nWAKFINEE SHARRA MAAA ASLAFT, WA A'SIMNEE MINAL IZDIYAADI FEE MA'SIYATIK, WA HABBIB ILAYYA TAA-A'TAKA WA MAA YUQARRIBUNEE MINKA WA YUZLIFUNEE I'NDAK\nand spare me the evil of what I have committed before, protect me from adding to my disobedience to You, and make dear to me Your obedience and whatever draws me near to You and brings me closer to You.\nسَيِّدِيْۤ اِلَيْكَ يَلْجَاُ الْهَارِبُ وَ مِنْكَ يَلْتَمِسُ الطَّالِبُ وَ عَلٰى كَرَمِكَ يُعَوِّلُ الْمُسْتَقِيْلُ التَّاۤئِبُ\nSAYYIDEE ILAYKA YALJA-UL HAARIB, WA MINKA YALTAMISUT TAALIB, WA A'LAA KARAMIKA YU-A'WWILUL MUSTAQEELUT TAAA-IB\nMy Master, to You the fugitive takes refuge, from You the seeker requests, and upon Your generosity the penitent seeking release relies.\nاَدَّبْتَ عِبَادَكَ بِالتَّكَرُّمِ وَ اَنْتَ اَكْرَمُ الْاَكْرَمِيْنَ وَ اَمَرْتَ بِالْعَفْوِ عِبَادَكَ وَ اَنْتَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ\nADDABTA I'BAADAKA BIT TAKARRUM, WA ANTA AKRAMUL AKRAMEEN, WA AMARTA BIL A'FWI I'BAADAK, WA ANTAL GHAFOORUR RAHEEM\nYou have taught Your servants generosity, and You are the most Generous of the generous; You have commanded Your servants to pardon, and You are the All-forgiving, the All-merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَلَا تَحْرِمْنِيْ مَا رَجَوْتُ مِنْ كَرَمِكَ وَ لَا تُؤْيِسْنِيْ مِنْ سَابِغِ نِعَمِكَ وَ لَا تُخَيِّبْنِيْ مِنْ جَزِيْلِ قِسَمِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA FALAA TAHRIMNEE MAA RAJAWTU MIN KARAMIK, WA LAA TU-YISNEE MIN SAABIGHI NI-A'MIK, WA LAA TUKHAYYIBNEE MIN JAZEELI QISAMIK\nO Allah, so do not deprive me of what I have hoped for from Your generosity, and do not make me despair of Your abundant blessings, and do not disappoint me of Your generous portion,\nفِيْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ لِاَهْلِ طَاعَتِكَ وَ اجْعَلْنِيْ فِيْ جُنَّةٍ مِنْ شِرَارِ بَرِيَّتِكَ\nFEE HAAZIHIL LAYLATI LI-AHLI TAA-A'TIK, WAJ-A'LNEE FEE JUNNATIM MIN SHIRAARI BARIYYATIK\nthat You grant this night to those who obey You, and place me in a shield against the wicked of Your creation.\nرَبِّ اِنْ لَمْ اَكُنْ مِنْ اَهْلِ ذٰلِكَ فَاَنْتَ اَهْلُ الْكَرَمِ وَ الْعَفْوِ وَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ\nRABBI IL LAM AKUM MIN AHLI ZAALIKA FA-ANTA AHLUL KARAMI WAL A'FWI WAL MAGHFIRAH\nMy Lord, if I am not worthy of that, then You are worthy of generosity, pardon, and forgiveness,\nوَ جُدْ عَلَيَّ بِمَاۤ اَنْتَ اَهْلُهُ لَا بِمَاۤ اَسْتَحِقُّهُ فَقَدْ حَسُنَ ظَنِّيْ بِكَ وَ تَحَقَّقَ رَجَاۤئِيْ لَكَ وَ عَلِقَتْ نَفْسِيْ بِكَرَمِكَ\nWA JUD A'LAYYA BIMAAA ANTA AHLUH, LAA BIMAAA ASTAHIQQUH, FAQAD HASUNA ZANNEE BIK, WA TAHAQQAQA RAJAAA-EE LAK, WA A'LIQAT NAFSEE BI-KARAMIK\nso be generous to me according to what befits You, not according to what I deserve — for my thought of You is good, my hope in You is firm, and my soul clings to Your generosity;\nفَاَنْتَ اَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ وَ اَكْرَمُ الْاَكْرَمِيْنَ\nFA-ANTA ARHAMUR RAAHIMEENA WA AKRAMUL AKRAMEEN\nfor You are the Most Merciful of the merciful and the most Generous of the generous.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَ اخْصُصْنِيْ مِنْ كَرَمِكَ بِجَزِيْلِ قِسَمِكَ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِعَفْوِكَ مِنْ عُقُوْبَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA WAKHSUSNEE MIN KARAMIKA BI-JAZEELI QISAMIK, WA A-U'ZU BI-A'FWIKA MIN U'QOOBATIK\nO Allah, favor me exclusively from Your generosity with a generous portion, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment,\nوَ اغْفِرْ لِيَ الذَّنْبَ الَّذِيْ يَحْبِسُ عَلَيَّ الْخُلُقَ وَ يُضَيِّقُ عَلَيَّ الرِّزْقَ\nWAGH FIR LEEYAZ ZAMBAL LAZEE YAHBISU A'LAYYAL KHULUQA WA YUDAYYIQU A'LAYYAR RIZQ\nand forgive me the sin that withholds good character from me and narrows my sustenance,\nحَتّٰىۤ اَقُوْمَ بِصَالِحِ رِضَاكَ وَ اَنْعَمَ بِجَزِيْلِ عَطَاۤئِكَ وَ اَسْعَدَ بِسَابِغِ نَعْمَاۤئِكَ\nHATTAA AQOOMA BI-SAALIHI RIDAAK, WA AN-A'MA BI-JAZEELI A'TAAA-IK, WA AS-A'DA BI-SAABIGHI NA'MAAA-IK\nso that I may stand upon what pleases You, enjoy Your generous giving, and be blessed by Your abundant favor.\nفَقَدْ لُذْتُ بِحَرَمِكَ وَ تَعَرَّضْتُ لِكَرَمِكَ وَ اسْتَعَذْتُ بِعَفْوِكَ مِنْ عُقُوْبَتِكَ وَ بِحِلْمِكَ مِنْ غَضَبِكَ\nFAQAD LUZTU BI-HARAMIK, WA TA-A'RRADTU LI-KARAMIK, WASTA-A'ZTU BI-A'FWIKA MIN U'QOOBATIK, WA BI-HILMIKA MIN GHADABIK\nI have indeed taken refuge in Your sanctuary, presented myself for Your generosity, and sought protection in Your pardon from Your punishment and in Your forbearance from Your wrath;\nفَجُدْ بِمَا سَاَلْتُكَ وَ اَنِلْ مَا الْتَمَسْتُ مِنْكَ اَسْاَلُكَ بِكَ لَا بِشَيْءٍ هُوَ اَعْظَمُ مِنْكَ\nFAJUD BIMAA SA-ALTUK, WA ANIL MAL TAMASTU MINK, AS-ALUKA BIKA LAA BI-SHAY-IN HUWA A'ZAMU MINK\nso grant me what I have asked You, and give me what I have sought from You; I ask You by You, not by anything greater than You.\nThen prostrate and repeat \"YAA RABB\" (O my Lord) twenty times, then \"YAA ALLAAH\" (O Allah) seven times, then \"LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAH\" (there is no power and no strength except with Allah) seven times, then \"MAA SHAAA-AL LAAH\" (what Allah wills) ten times, then \"LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAH\" (there is no strength except with Allah) ten times, then invoke Allah's blessings upon the Holy Prophet and make your requests. By Allah, even if your requests were as numerous as raindrops, Allah would grant them all out of His generosity and favor.\nEleventh: Shaykh al-Tusi and Shaykh al-Kaf'ami say it is fitting to say the following this night, recommended right after the Shaf' Prayer at the last hours of the night:\nاِلٰهِيْ تَعَرَّضَ لَكَ فِي هٰذَا اللَّيْلِ الْمُتَعَرِّضُوْنَ وَ قَصَدَكَ الْقَاصِدُوْنَ وَ اَمَّلَ فَضْلَكَ وَ مَعْرُوْفَكَ الطَّالِبُوْنَ\nILAAHEE TA-A'RRADA LAKA FEE HAAZAL LAYLIL MUTA-A'RRIDOON, WA QASADAKAL QAASIDOON, WA AMMALA FADLAKA WA MA'ROOFAKAT TAALIBOON\nMy God, tonight those who seek You have presented themselves before You, those who intend You have set their aim upon You, and those who ask have hoped for Your bounty and Your kindness,\nوَ لَكَ فِيْ هٰذَا اللَّيْلِ نَفَحَاتٌ وَ جَوَاۤئِزُ وَ عَطَايَا وَ مَوَاهِبُ تَمُنُّ بِهَا عَلٰى مَنْ تَشَاۤءُ مِنْ عِبَادِكَ وَ تَمْنَعُهَا مَنْ لَمْ تَسْبِقْ لَهُ الْعِنَايَةُ مِنْكَ\nWA LAKA FEE HAAZAL LAYLI NAFAHAATUW WA JAWAAA-IZU WA A'TAAYAA WA MAWAAHIBU TAMUNNU BIHAA A'LAA MAN TASHAAA-O MIN I'BAADIK, WA TAMNA-U'HAA MAL LAM TASBIQ LAHUL I'NAAYATU MINK\nand Yours, on this night, are gusts of grace, rewards, gifts, and endowments which You bestow upon whomever You will of Your servants, and withhold from whoever Your prior care has not preceded.\nوَ هَاۤ اَنَا ذَا عُبَيْدُكَ الْفَقِيْرُ اِلَيْكَ الْمُؤَمِّلُ فَضْلَكَ وَ مَعْرُوْفَكَ\nWA HAAA ANAA ZAA U'BAYDUKAL FAQEERU ILAYKAL MU-AMMILU FADLAKA WA MA'ROOFAK\nAnd here am I, Your humble servant, in need of You, hoping for Your bounty and Your kindness;\nفَاِنْ كُنْتَ يَا مَوْلَايَ تَفَضَّلْتَ فِيْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ عَلٰىۤ اَحَدٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ وَ عُدْتَ عَلَيْهِ بِعَاۤئِدَةٍ مِنْ عَطْفِكَ\nFA-IN KUNTA YAA MAWLAAYA TAFADDALTA FEE HAAZIHIL LAYLATI A'LAA AHADIM MIN KHALQIK, WA U'DTA A'LAYHI BI-A'AA-IDATIM MIN A'TFIK\nso if, O my Master, You have shown favor tonight to any of Your creatures and returned to him with a portion of Your kindness,\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ الْخَيِّرِيْنَ الْفَاضِلِيْنَ وَ جُدْ عَلَيَّ بِطَوْلِكَ وَ مَعْرُوْفِكَ يَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIW WA AALI MUHAMMADIN AT-TAYYIBEENAT TAAHIREENAL KHAYYIREENAL FAADILEEN, WA JUD A'LAYYA BI-TAWLIKA WA MA'ROOFIKA YAA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\nthen bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad — the good, the pure, the excellent, the virtuous — and be generous to me with Your grace and Your kindness, O Lord of the worlds.\nوَ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ وَ اٰلِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ وَ سَلَّمَ تَسْلِيْمًا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ حَمِيْدٌ مَجِيْدٌ\nWA SALLAL LAAHO A'LAA MUHAMMADIN KHAATAMIN NABIYYEENA WA AALIHIT TAAHIREENA WA SALLAMA TASLEEMAA, INNAL LAAHA HAMEEDUM MAJEED\nAnd Allah's blessings be upon Muhammad, the seal of the Prophets, and his pure Household, and abundant peace; verily Allah is Praiseworthy, All-glorious.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَدْعُوْكَ كَمَاۤ اَمَرْتَ فَاسْتَجِبْ لِيْ كَمَا وَعَدْتَ اِنَّكَ لَا تُخْلِفُ الْمِيْعَادَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AD-U'WKA KAMAA AMART, FASTAJIB LEE KAMAA WA-A'DT, INNAKA LAA TUKHLIFUL MEE-A'AAD\nO Allah, I call upon You as You have commanded; so answer me as You have promised, for verily You do not break Your promise.\nTwelfth: it is recommended to say the supplication narrated by Shaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid Ibn Tawus after each two units of the Night Prayer, the Shaf' Prayer, and the Witr Prayer.\nThirteenth: it is recommended to perform the prostrations and supplications reported from the Holy Prophet (s). Shaykh al-Tusi narrates, on the authority of Hammad ibn Isa, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a): it was the fifteenth night of Shaban when the Holy Prophet (s) was with his wife Aisha. At midnight the Prophet left the bed; when Aisha awoke and could not find him, she grew jealous, thinking he had gone to another wife, and rose, putting on her cloak — made of neither silk, linen, nor cotton, but camel hair. She searched the rooms of his other wives but found him prostrate on the ground like a discarded garment. Drawing near, she heard him saying:\nسَجَدَ لَكَ سَوَادِيْ وَ خَيَالِيْ وَ اٰمَنَ بِكَ فُؤَادِيْ هٰذِهِ يَدَايَ وَ مَا جَنَيْتُهُ عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ يَا عَظِيْمُ تُرْجٰى لِكُلِّ عَظِيْمٍ اِغْفِرْ لِيَ الْعَظِيْمَ فَاِنَّهُ لَا يَغْفِرُ الذَّنْبَ الْعَظِيْمَ اِلَّا الرَّبُّ الْعَظِيْمُ\nSAJADA LAKA SAWAADEE WA KHAYAALEE WA AAMANA BIKA FU-AADEE, HAAZIHI YADAAYA WA MAA JANAYTUHU A'LAA NAFSEE, YAA A'ZEEMU TURJAA LI-KULLI A'ZEEM, IGHFIR LIYAL A'ZEEM, FA-INNAHU LAA YAGHFIRUZ ZAMBAL A'ZEEMA ILLAR RABBUL A'ZEEM\nMy silhouette and my shadow have prostrated to You, and my heart has believed in You; these are my two hands and what I have wrought against myself. O Most Great, You are hoped for at every great matter — forgive me the great sin, for none forgives a great sin except the Great Lord.\nThe Prophet then raised his head and prostrated again, saying:\nاَعُوْذُ بِنُوْرِ وَجْهِكَ الَّذِيْۤ اَضَاۤءَتْ لَهُ السَّمَاوَاتُ وَ الْاَرَضُوْنَ وَ انْكَشَفَتْ لَهُ الظُّلُمَاتُ وَ صَلَحَ عَلَيْهِ اَمْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَ الْاٰخِرِيْنَ\nA-U'ZU BI-NOORI WAJHIKAL LAZEEE ADAAA-AT LAHUS SAMAAWAATU WAL ARADOON, WAN KASHAFAT LAHUZ ZULUMAAT, WA SALAHA A'LAYHI AMRUL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN\nI seek refuge in the light of Your Countenance, by which the heavens and the earths were illumined, the darkness was dispelled, and the affairs of the first and the last were set right,\nمِنْ فُجْاَةِ نَقِمَتِكَ وَ مِنْ تَحْوِيْلِ عَافِيَتِكَ وَ مِنْ زَوَالِ نِعْمَتِكَ\nMIN FUJ-ATI NAQIMATIK, WA MIN TAHWEELI A'AAFIYATIK, WA MIN ZAWAALI NI'MATIK\nfrom the sudden onset of Your vengeance, from the turning away of Your well-being, and from the vanishing of Your blessing.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْزُقْنِيْ قَلْبًا تَقِيًّا نَقِيًّا وَ مِنَ الشِّرْكِ بَرِيْئًا لَا كَافِرًا وَ لَا شَقِيًّا\nALLAAHUMMAR ZUQNEE QALBAN TAQIYYAN NAQIYYAW WA MINASH SHIRKI BAREE-AL LAA KAAFIRAW WA LAA SHAQIYYAA\nO Allah, grant me a heart that is God-fearing and pure, free of association, neither disbelieving nor wretched.\nThe Prophet then pressed his face to the ground and said:\nعَفَّرْتُ وَجْهِيْ فِيْ التُّرَابِ وَ حُقَّ لِيْۤ اَنْ اَسْجُدَ لَكَ\nA'FFARTU WAJHEE FIT TURAAB WA HUQQA LEE AN ASJUDA LAK\nI have laid my face in the dust, and it is only right that I prostrate to You.\nWhen the Prophet finished and turned back to bed, Aisha hurried ahead and reached it first. Hearing her fast breathing, he wondered aloud, then said, \"Do you know what night this is? This is the mid-Shaban night. On it shares of provision are distributed, lifetimes are decided, and pilgrims of the coming year are appointed. Allah, this night, forgives as many of His creatures as the hairs on the horses of the Kalb tribe, and sends angels down to the earth, to Makkah.\"\nFourteenth: it is recommended to offer the famous [Namaz of Jafar-e-Tayyaar](F11), as narrated by Shaykh al-Tusi from Imam al-Rida (a).\nFifteenth: it is recommended to offer the many prayers dedicated to this night. One, reported by Abu-Yahya al-San'ani and thirty other trustworthy narrators from Imam Muhammad al-Baqir and Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a): on the mid-Shaban night, offer a four-unit prayer, reciting [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Ikhlas](A116) a hundred times in each unit. On finishing, say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اِلَيْكَ فَقِيْرٌ وَ مِنْ عَذَابِكَ خَاۤئِفٌ مُسْتَجِيْرٌ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ILAYKA FAQEERUW WA MIN A'ZAABIKA KHAAA-IFUM MUSTAJEER\nO Allah, I am in need of You, and fearful of Your punishment, seeking refuge,\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تُبَدِّلْ اِسْمِيْ وَ لَا تُغَيِّرْ جِسْمِيْ وَ لَا تَجْهَدْ بَلَاۤئِيْ وَ لَا تُشْمِتْ بِيْۤ اَعْدَاۤئِيْ\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TUBADDIL ISMEE WA LAA TUGHAYYIR JISMEE WA LAA TAJHAD BALAAA-EE WA LAA TUSHMIT BEE A'DAAA-EE\nO Allah, do not change my name, do not alter my body, do not intensify my trial, and do not let my enemies gloat over me;\nاَعُوْذُ بِعَفْوِكَ مِنْ عِقَابِكَ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِرَحْمَتِكَ مِنْ عَذَابِكَ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِرِضَاكَ مِنْ سَخَطِكَ وَ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْكَ\nA-U'ZU BI-A'FWIKA MIN I'QAABIK, WA A-U'ZU BI-RAHMATIKA MIN A'ZAABIK, WA A-U'ZU BI-RIDAAKA MIN SAKHATIK, WA A-U'ZU BIKA MINK\nI seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, I seek refuge in Your mercy from Your chastisement, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in You from You.\nجَلَّ ثَنَاۤؤُكَ اَنْتَ كَمَا اَثْنَيْتَ عَلٰى نَفْسِكَ وَ فَوْقَ مَا يَقُوْلُ الْقَاۤئِلُوْنَ\nJALLA THANAAA-UKA ANTA KAMAA ATHNAYTA A'LAA NAFSIKA WA FAWQA MAA YAQOOLUL QAAA-ILOON\nExalted is Your praise; You are as You have praised Yourself, and above what any speaker can say.\nTraditions have set a great reward for whoever offers a hundred-unit prayer this night, reciting Surah al-Faatehah once and Surah al-Ikhlas ten times in each unit. It was mentioned earlier, in the rites of Rajab, that a six-unit prayer is also recommended, reciting Surah al-Faatehah, Surah Yasin, Surah al-Mulk, and Surah al-Ikhlas in each unit."
